# wp-content/plugins/ is bind-mounted as ONE folder so WordPress can see
# everything in a single flat directory, but only YOUR custom plugins are
# tracked by git. Everything else (third-party plugins, whatever gets
# extracted from init-data/plugins*.tar.gz, anything installed from the WP
# admin) is ignored by default.
#
# Convention: every locally-developed plugin folder must be prefixed with
# "acme-" (rename to your own project/company prefix, e.g. "acme-" ->
# "yourco-"). That's the ONLY thing that decides whether a plugin folder is
# versioned or not - no need to keep editing this file as you add plugins.
 
# 1. Ignore everything in this directory...
*
 
# 2. ...except this file itself...
!.gitignore
 
# 3. ...and any custom plugin folder matching the prefix (and its contents).
!acme-*/
!acme-*/**